From b310ab90223715153414d533557aa1165b4eb526 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: woahwhattheheck <293286387+woahwhattheheck@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 05:19:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(complete): Respect require_equals in native
 completions

With `require_equals`, the parser only accepts a value attached with `=`.
Native completions still treated the next argument as the value
(`--format <TAB>` offered values) and attached short values without `=`
(`-F<TAB>` offered `-Fjson`).

Now
- flags that require a value complete to `--format=` / `-F=`
- the next argument is not treated as the value
- short values are attached with `=` and values attached without `=` are
  not completed
- an optional value (`num_args(0..=1)`, like `--color[=<WHEN>]`) is only
  taken after `=`, so the flag stays complete on its own and any following
  short flags are parsed as flags, matching the parser
---
 clap_complete/src/engine/complete.rs    | 72 +++++++++++++++++++------
 clap_complete/tests/testsuite/engine.rs | 31 ++++++-----
 2 files changed, 74 insertions(+), 29 deletions(-)

diff --git a/clap_complete/src/engine/complete.rs b/clap_complete/src/engine/complete.rs
index f8e0e207..95c2d7b7 100644
--- a/clap_complete/src/engine/complete.rs
+++ b/clap_complete/src/engine/complete.rs
@@ -90,7 +90,7 @@ pub fn complete(
                 });
 
